The [[Bloodthorne]] is a [[Weapon]] normally obtained by combining a [[Hungry Blade]] with a [[Thorn Whip]]. On hit, it uses a {{icon/regeneration}} to gain both a {{icon/vampirism}} and a {{icon/spikes}}, and it scales damage with both {{icon/vampirism}} and {{icon/spikes}}.

The [[Bloodthorne]] is better in almost every way compared to both the [[Hungry Blade]] and [[Thorn Whip]].

Compared to the [[Hungry Blade]], the [[Bloodthorne]] does cost significantly more stamina, but has the strong upside of scaling its damage rather than its maximum damage, making it a much more damaging weapon, especially when considering the additional {{icon/spikes}} gained and {{icon/spikes}}-scaling.

Compared to the [[Thorn Whip]], the [[Bloodthorne]] is smaller and of a much less awkward shape. As long as there's enough {{icon/regeneration}} to feed the [[Bloodthorne]] on every hit, it will gain even more {{icon/spikes}} and deal more damage than the [[Thorn Whip]], on top of all the {{icon/vampirism}}-based benefits, since it attacks faster.

Overall, the [[Bloodthorne]] is a great end-game weapon, since it scales off of two different buffs that have a high potential to be stacked.

[[Ranger]]s can add [[Wisp]]s on [[Bloodthorne]] to increase the {{icon/spikes}} gained from dealing damage.

[[Adventurer]]s have the unique option to craft the [[Impractically Large Bloodthorne]] by combining a [[Bloodthorne]] and an [[Impractically Large Greatsword]] using a [[Twine]]. It's essentially a huger but slower [[Bloodthorne]] with drastically amped-up effects.
